 we conclude that when $t=0,$ the tangent to the curve is horizontal." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317625 #edb/ref 1080 "-4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317625 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317625 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "12952b5e-889f-54cc-a122-5d50215660f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318301 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{2}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318301 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318301 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dc186f89-e80b-5eb4-a0f9-50d2a3804e90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318471 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186317625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318471 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318471 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318471 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186317625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318471 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "162eb28c-9915-5e71-854b-15570d6140d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318573 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186318301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318573 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318573 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318573 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186318301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318573 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "45248884-e4ee-5dd3-b87d-9707883c9d1c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319374 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319374 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319374 #edb/ref 1069 "q-350359" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319374 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319374 #edb/ref 1071 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}t+\\frac{1}{2},\\,y={t}^{3}+7{t}^{2}+8t,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is horizontal. Do not round the answers.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the tangent to the curve is horizontal at $t=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $t=$\n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319374 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8ca39289-4112-5812-a40f-16d38e719123" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319374 #edb/ref 1074 "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is horizontal if ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${x}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2t+\\frac{1}{2},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2}+14t+8\n$$\n\nSolving ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}+14t+8 & =0 \\\\ (3t+2)(t+4) & =0 \\\\ t & =-4,-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(-4) & =2(-4)+\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{15}{2}\\ne 0, \\\\ {x}^{′}(-\\frac{2}{3}) & =2(-\\frac{2}{3})+\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{5}{6}\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the tangent to the curve is indeed horizontal at $t=-4$ and $t=-\\frac{2}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408166 #edb/ref 10 :answer-field.type/checkbox #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186429627 #edb/ref 1030 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429627 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 799->3557. All account evid